Z||000000||jhogans||10-18-1999||10:00 AM||||Check out this interesting Fiero - <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/warberfs.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/warberfs.htm</A>  -<P>Tell me what you think with a 1 to 10 point rating with 1 being the lowest and 10 being the highest.<P>I must say that this car deserves a 10.  The 450 HP V8 alone gets the 10  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  This is definetly a Mustang Killer!!!!!!!<P>BTW, I'm not sure on the rules of this Forum but are these kinds of post welcomed?  I hate to bog down the forum with non-helpful info if it is not welcomed.<P>Talk to you guys later.  Gotta get to work.||||reg||14
Z||000001||87GT||10-18-1999||01:35 PM||||I give the person that went through all the trouble of the mods a 10 for patience.  Personally, I dont like to see a fiero all chopped and modified.  I like em all original.  As far as a rating of 1-10 on its looks, I give it about a 8.  Making it a notchback style when it was originally a fastback GT, is kinda of strange to me.  I must say that I do give the motor a 10 also! 8-)||||reg||1
Z||000002||RZURCTN||10-18-1999||02:22 PM||||I'll have to agree with 87GT.  I like the orininal styling of the Fiero.  If you do some internal mods that's great!  But why chop up a perfectly good Fiero?  ||||reg||13
Z||000003||Eddie||10-18-1999||05:24 PM||||COOL CAR I to like to see stock fiero,s but that fiero is way to cool. ITS (10)MY BOOK ||||reg||14
