Z||000013||JIM GOOSE||10-19-1999||08:45 AM||||Those are certainly wild looking cars,both of them. They might be a little cramped though, seems to me that legroom is worse than headroom in the stock Fiero. Had a Lotus Europa before I got this car and it was more comfortable by far, once you got into it. My left leg feels like it is in a slightly odd position much of the time.||||reg||10
Z||000014||fiero56||10-19-1999||04:10 PM||||In city driving my formula seems to have plenty of leg room, but once I've been on the highway for about an hour, that dead pedal just seems way too close.  When the road is empty, I just take off my left shoe and rest my foot behind the clutch pedal.  I get to stretch out as far as I would like to then.||||reg||1
Z||000015||spike||10-20-1999||12:51 PM||||Next summer I plan on making a new spoiler/ground effects kit to help improve the look of the Fiero GT (not that it needs it). I will also have a custom sub box to fit 2 10" subs with no loss of seat travel or interior space. Till then..... ||||reg||1
